  "content": {
    "id": "v2-97400-p42-practice-slot-3-upper-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "A food truck at a Brisbane market pays $\\$900$ for the stall plus $\\$3.50$ for ingredients for every serve.\nEach serve sells for $\\$10$, but the market keeps 20% of all sales.\nWrite two equations, one for costs and one for revenue.\nFind how many serves must be sold for the food truck to break-even (cost = revenue).",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$C=900+3.5n$, $R=8n$. Break-even at 200 serves.",
      "worked": "Let $n$ be the number of serves produced and sold, and let $C$ and $R$ be the cost and revenue in dollars. The truck keeps 80% of each $\\$10$ sale, which is $\\$8$.\n$$\\begin{align*}C&=900+3.5n\\\\R&=8n\\end{align*}$$\nAt break-even, $C=R$.\n$$\\begin{align*}900+3.5n&=8n\\\\4.5n&=900\\\\n&=200\\end{align*}$$\nThe food truck must sell 200 serves to break even.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": null
  },
